   "description": "Envy is the pain felt at another person's good fortune — not simply wanting what they have but resenting the fact that they have it. The Hebrew root (qana) covers both the negative form (jealousy, envy) and a positive form (zealous devotion); God is described as jealous in the positive sense. What distinguishes envy from desire is the element of resentment: envy is grieved by another's advantage, not merely moved by one's own lack. It is one of the most socially destructive inner states.",
